    {
      "id": "_0a9tuXU0lxDudJfTiOnN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1297.862619186612,
      "y": 417.18680677174586,
      "width": 362.94122314453125,
      "height": 419.2206654991244,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2066441533,
      "version": 890,
      "versionNonce": 1649225555,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1775414148968,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "step 2: WE NEED TO MAKE TWO GROUPS\nby \"finding where a and b differ at which bit\"\n\nso, we have \"xor = 6\" as (a ^ b)\nand we need to extract a and b from it\n\nwe know, a != b. so at least one bit in the xor is set\nso if we make two groups, such that each group will contain\none answer,\n\nwe can do that, by taking:\nbit_diff = 1\n\nxor = 6 = 110\n\nwhile((xor & bit_diff) == 0) bit_diff = bit_diff << 1; \n\nso,  untill (xor & bit_diff) == 0 we left shift 1\nand if we find first 0 in xor\n\n110\n001\n-----\n111 != 0\n",
      "fontSize": 13.41506129597198,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "step 2: WE NEED TO MAKE TWO GROUPS\nby \"finding where a and b differ at which bit\"\n\nso, we have \"xor = 6\" as (a ^ b)\nand we need to extract a and b from it\n\nwe know, a != b. so at least one bit in the xor is set\nso if we make two groups, such that each group will contain\none answer,\n\nwe can do that, by taking:\nbit_diff = 1\n\nxor = 6 = 110\n\nwhile((xor & bit_diff) == 0) bit_diff = bit_diff << 1; \n\nso,  untill (xor & bit_diff) == 0 we left shift 1\nand if we find first 0 in xor\n\n110\n001\n-----\n111 != 0\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
